WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.003
- Hi, guys.

00:00:01.003 --> 00:00:04.410
It's Justine and I'm making a video.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.243
It's weird.

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:06.810
Everything is just so weird right now

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.300
and I cannot reiterate enough

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.150
whatever you're feeling
right now about everything.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.530
Your feelings are valid

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.300
because everyone is
feeling some sort of way

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.996
and I don't know how we deal with it

00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:22.650
but the one thing that I have realized

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.680
is the internet is coming
together as a community,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.150
to really just uplift people,

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.690
and I think that's so important right now

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.180
and not just on the internet,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.980
in your community is where
you live, neighborhoods,

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.190
people are helping each other.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.610
And I've even reached out
to some of my neighbors

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.160
and asked if there's
anything that I can do

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.030
because I don't know what else to do.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.810
I am actually quarantining myself.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.610
I'm taking those precautions.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.180
The number one thing right now,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.150
is people who don't have symptoms,

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.950
they have this and they're
giving it to people

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.230
not even knowing that they have it.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.790
So that's why all these
precautions are in place.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.100
I'm not gonna go into it,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.850
but I wanted to just show you guys

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.710
some of the tweets that I got today,

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.543
because this morning,

00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:06.090
I was really having a really
hard time with everything.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.360
I was in my closet, trying
to put laundry away,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.690
and I just started crying

00:01:11.249 --> 00:01:13.220
and I want to help.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.310
I don't know what to do.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.450
I think so many of us want to.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.521
And as somebody who does have an audience,

00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:19.980
the things that we say,

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.580
I hate the term influencer
more than anything,

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.330
but in this sense,
that's what we're doing.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:27.040
I follow a lot of different people.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.060
And the past several weeks,

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.750
I'm following these people,

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.980
thinking that the things that they say

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.720
are things that I can trust,

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.360
and it turns out

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.730
a lot of people have retweeted
a lot of false information.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.520
And like I said in a previous video,

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.000
that's something that I never wanna do.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.160
I never want to be providing
you guys false information.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.620
So I tweeted this this morning,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.330
just asking what can we,

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.290
as people who you watch, as influencers,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.790
what can we do?

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.990
What do you want from us?

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.770
I'd also been talking a bunch
of my other internet friends

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.920
who are also making YouTube videos

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.080
and we kind of all have the same feeling,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.900
like we wanna do something
but we don't know what to do.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.310
Do we keep making videos?

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.836
And that's such an internal conflict

00:02:05.836 --> 00:02:08.500
'cause we wanna be sensitive
to what's happening.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.770
And the overwhelming response
that I got to this tweet

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:12.967
was people saying,

00:02:12.967 --> 00:02:15.367
"We need you guys more than ever right now

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.897
"to keep making the content.

00:02:16.897 --> 00:02:18.860
"Don't continually keep
talking about this."

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.310
Because that's what the news is doing.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.920
We're being inundated
by so much information.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.860
I think just following
the CDC and websites

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.630
that are actually giving
us truthful information

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.960
is really the number one thing.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.250
They're telling us to wash our hands,

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.620
stay inside because you don't
know if you could have it.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.850
You could be spreading it to someone

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.180
who then gives it to their family.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.530
It hurts just to see people
not taking it seriously.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.970
But this thread was so
incredibly refreshing,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.660
which is why I wanted to just
sit here and thank you guys

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.500
for your responses

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.690
and I wanna read some to you

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.210
because if you are somebody
who is making YouTube videos

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.267
or making any type of content online,

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:54.600
these were really,

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.820
it was really helpful
for me to also read this

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.310
and just see what you guys want from us.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:02.490
So I'm gonna start with Steven
who is also from Pittsburgh

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.605
and a gamer and he's
absolutely incredible.

00:03:04.605 --> 00:03:06.520
This is what he had to say.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.417
He said, "I honestly believe

00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:09.277
"that the best thing that
we can do as influencers,

00:03:09.277 --> 00:03:10.787
"no matter, whether you have a hundred

00:03:10.787 --> 00:03:12.207
"or a million followers,

00:03:12.207 --> 00:03:15.217
"is to keep creating the kind
of content that you want.

00:03:15.217 --> 00:03:16.847
"Our obligation is to our community,

00:03:16.847 --> 00:03:18.967
"to be the best shepherds we know how.

00:03:18.967 --> 00:03:20.660
"That's all anyone can ask of us."

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.340
And I think this is really important,

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.030
the fact that he's
saying it doesn't matter

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.322
if you have a hundred
or a million followers,

00:03:26.322 --> 00:03:28.583
even if you just have one or two,

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:32.060
that's some who could
potentially need help,

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.920
that's why I'm stressing to you guys,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.880
reach out to your friends.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.958
People that you may not
have talked to in a while.

00:03:36.958 --> 00:03:38.394
Ask them if they're okay.

00:03:38.394 --> 00:03:40.250
Ask them if their family's okay.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.430
And ask them if anybody needs anything.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.740
'Cause you might have something,

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.770
an abundance of maybe some toilet paper

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.570
that you could share with
somebody who needs it.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.990
This was a great tweet from James.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.060
So I really appreciate it.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.337
He said to "follow your heart.

00:03:51.337 --> 00:03:54.590
"People need information and
they need entertainment."

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.580
Even myself.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.000
I have been spending a lot of time,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.300
trying to just find content to watch

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.110
and all people are talking about is this.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.930
So I just wanna reiterate,

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.930
this is gonna be my last
video about the whole subject.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.160
I mean, I'm gonna be talking about it

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.220
but I don't wanna make this
overabundance of content,

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.550
just saying the same things

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.720
that you guys are hearing on the news

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.760
because clearly that's
not what you guys want,

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.360
but I just want you to know that

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.600
this is a worldwide thing.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.680
We're all going through this.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.130
Not a single person

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.630
who feels like they're
the only one doing this.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.900
They're not.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.770
It's really really crazy.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.370
I'm still processing.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.870
I don't even know.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.800
I don't know, I don't know, we don't know.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.367
Rene Ritchie says, "Providing
compassion and escapism.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.737
"Information where we can,
entertainment where needed.

00:04:42.737 --> 00:04:44.727
"Helping, never exploiting.

00:04:44.727 --> 00:04:46.527
"'Until such time as the world ends,

00:04:46.527 --> 00:04:48.900
"'we will act as though
it intends to spin on.'"

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:49.810
Which it does.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.720
And it was really such
a weird thing to see

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.430
that Apple had just announced
a bunch of new products

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.730
and when you think about it,

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.690
they have to.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.760
People still have to have jobs
after all of this is over.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.880
Apple's just a massive company.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.350
So many people work there.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.950
And this isn't just Apple.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.350
All companies have to try to keep going

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.880
for the sake of their employees.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.349
For the sake of those people's families.

00:05:13.349 --> 00:05:17.280
So, whatever after
this, our new normal is.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.310
That's what it's gonna be.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.450
It's gonna be a new normal

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.260
but I'm incredibly confident
that no matter what,

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.600
we're gonna figure it out.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.490
People adapt.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.790
And I think that a lot of us

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.660
are a lot stronger than we realize,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.410
and I think it's something like this,

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:34.220
that we really can use this
to create a better community,

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.510
realize things that are important,

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:39.130
and really just reevaluate
our entire lives

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.440
'cause that's definitely
something that I've been doing.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.900
And I think in the end,

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.870
it's gonna be a very positive thing.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.030
It might take a while

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.790
but I feel like we're all
gonna be so much better

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.563
coming out of this and surviving.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.370
Rebecca says, "Being honest."

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.150
I think that's incredibly important

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.757
because we can't be
spreading misinformation.

00:06:00.757 --> 00:06:01.677
"Everyone should do their best

00:06:01.677 --> 00:06:04.247
"to spread word of proper
quarantine protocols,

00:06:04.247 --> 00:06:07.017
"to be serious about the
situation, without panic,

00:06:07.017 --> 00:06:08.347
"stay firm about doing the right thing

00:06:08.347 --> 00:06:10.437
"for neighbors, friends,
family, without being negative,

00:06:10.437 --> 00:06:13.080
"dispel misinformation,
link good resources."

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.050
Definitely, a truth.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.370
I think just linking good
resources is very important.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:17.960
Just be careful that you are actually

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.627
linking something that is legitimate.

00:06:19.627 --> 00:06:20.547
"I think influencers

00:06:20.547 --> 00:06:22.207
"should be providing
entertainment right now

00:06:22.207 --> 00:06:23.987
"of all the things they love the most.

00:06:23.987 --> 00:06:25.617
"It'll give people an escape from the news

00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:27.107
"and everything that's going on."

00:06:27.107 --> 00:06:28.607
"Influencers should keep
making their content.

00:06:28.607 --> 00:06:29.837
"We need the distraction.

00:06:29.837 --> 00:06:31.967
"Just a little distraction and some videos

00:06:31.967 --> 00:06:33.310
"could help us on that end."

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:34.750
Working from home is not an easy thing.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.070
So if any of you guys,

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.940
this is something new to you,

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:40.934
that you've never done before,
it is incredibly difficult.

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:43.480
I have been basically working from home

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.120
for 13 or 14 years now.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.040
Obviously, in those years I've
been able to sort of set up

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.120
a little office space,

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.080
and separate my work home life.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.440
But it's still, it's all one.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.160
Everything just mixes together.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.220
So my biggest advice to
somebody who is struggling,

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.650
if there's any way,

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.410
even if you can just,

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.810
mark off a bit of the house

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.700
that is a no work zone,

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.860
that's gonna be so important,

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.190
whether it's your bedroom or the kitchen,

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.330
it's like no phones in the
kitchen or no laptops here.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.793
Just setting those small little boundaries

00:07:14.793 --> 00:07:16.930
for me has been very helpful,

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:17.763
and I think that

00:07:17.763 --> 00:07:19.750
for somebody that's kind
of getting thrown into this

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:20.690
for the first time,

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.050
maybe it'll help you, maybe it won't.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.640
I think you guys will
all quickly figure out

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.060
what works and what doesn't.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.187
Craig says, "Honestly, carry on as normal.

00:07:29.187 --> 00:07:31.427
"I think everyone would be
grateful for a distraction.

00:07:31.427 --> 00:07:33.277
"I wanna see your optimism and excitement

00:07:33.277 --> 00:07:34.407
"over brightly colored tech.

00:07:34.407 --> 00:07:35.360
"Keep doing you."

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.690
This also got me thinking,

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:39.310
talking about the new
iPad, and the MacBook,

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.040
and all of these new tech things

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:42.560
that are gonna be coming out.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.210
People are gonna have way
less disposable income

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.560
to spend on high-priced gadgets.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.110
So reviews are going to be so important

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.193
because you don't wanna be
wasting any bit of extra money

00:07:55.193 --> 00:07:58.310
on something that you don't
think is gonna be worth it.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.950
And obviously, I think reviews
are very important overall,

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.607
but now more than ever,

00:08:02.607 --> 00:08:06.400
you don't wanna leave
anything out to chance.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.800
You need to know,

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.910
I wanna know.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.740
I don't even wanna be spending extra money

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.720
on products to review

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.980
that could potentially
not even be worth it.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.650
It probably comes as a surprise

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:19.500
that I do buy a lot of
the tech that I review.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.770
I mean, I'm very lucky
that sometimes companies

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:22.810
will send things.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:27.170
I would say 70% of the time

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:28.527
I buy a lot of it.

00:08:28.527 --> 00:08:29.997
This one, I really like.

00:08:29.997 --> 00:08:32.137
"I'm a YouTuber with 300 plus subscribers.

00:08:32.137 --> 00:08:33.247
"In my opinion, at this time,

00:08:33.247 --> 00:08:36.457
"what we can do is just keep
going as we always have done.

00:08:36.457 --> 00:08:37.627
"Also this would be a good time

00:08:37.627 --> 00:08:39.387
"to share a skill with your followers.

00:08:39.387 --> 00:08:41.057
"Help them develop new skills

00:08:41.057 --> 00:08:43.330
"and encourage them to
be creative and busy."

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.600
And that's something that
I cannot stress enough.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.120
Just keeping busy.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:50.260
Working out, I think, is
gonna be very important

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.270
for so many people

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.470
and it's something that I
definitely struggle with,

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.950
because I love group workout classes.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:58.150
I love going to group yoga classes,

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:00.160
getting into jujitsu in the past two years

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.170
has been something that is so,

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.810
it's been basically
just a place that I go,

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.807
that I can be myself,

00:09:07.807 --> 00:09:09.930
not have to worry about anything,

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:11.160
and learn and train,

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.800
and now that I haven't
been able to do that,

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.540
trying to find ways to keep motivated

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.720
and work out at home.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.199
I don't know if you guys have
been paying much attention

00:09:17.199 --> 00:09:18.110
to some of the things

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:19.320
that a lot of companies have been doing,

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.912
but I've been a huge fan
of Peloton, not sponsored.

00:09:21.912 --> 00:09:24.428
They have a really great digital app,

00:09:24.428 --> 00:09:26.930
and they're giving people 90 days free

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.390
and I am so excited about this

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:29.760
because I love this app so much.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.350
They have so many incredible classes,

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.830
their yoga classes are amazing.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:34.700
So the one upside to a lot of this

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:35.680
is a lot of these companies

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.160
are giving away some
incredible things for free.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.030
I usually go to CorePower Yoga.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.557
They have some free online classes.

00:09:41.557 --> 00:09:42.960
It's also been so amazing

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.440
to see so many jujitsu gyms

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.820
giving away their curriculum for free.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.210
Everyone is just kind of banding together

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:50.840
and really just trying
to get through this.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:51.940
It's also fascinating

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:53.350
because I've had a lot of people

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:54.261
reach out and say,

00:09:54.261 --> 00:09:58.110
"What's the best way to
create online content?"

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.770
So that's something that
I'm also considering,

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.640
is if I can put together a little video

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:04.940
for people who have never
made anything online before.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:08.160
Here's just a few simple easy steps

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.867
and things that you can
do to start creating.

00:10:09.867 --> 00:10:11.571
'cause it's a whole 'nother world

00:10:11.571 --> 00:10:12.404
and it's just something

00:10:12.404 --> 00:10:14.450
that I've really been doing my whole life.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:17.950
And to throw a company or a small business

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.210
into now having to move
everything to digital,

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:21.180
I can't even imagine.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.000
I think it's incredibly difficult.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.150
So I think that's also something

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:25.760
that a lot of us tech people can do,

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:27.050
offer our expertise

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.660
and somehow help some of these businesses

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.400
through the trying times of
trying to create content online

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.610
because it's not easy.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.520
It's not easy at all.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.500
And I think people are
finally realizing that.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.710
So if there's anything you
guys would like to see,

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:42.703
or you think that would be
helpful to people, let me know.

00:10:42.703 --> 00:10:44.597
"What I need right is from influencers

00:10:44.597 --> 00:10:45.997
"to keep doing what you're doing.

00:10:45.997 --> 00:10:47.457
"My life has been interrupted enough,

00:10:47.457 --> 00:10:48.907
"no need for changes."

00:10:48.907 --> 00:10:50.163
"To put people's mind on something else.

00:10:50.163 --> 00:10:51.697
